  "question": {
    "text": "The probability that a randomly selected <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>digit number belongs to the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is a&nbsp;multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>}</mo></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Total two-digit numbers is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn></math></p><p>So, total number of cases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>90</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Here, the term&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;should be&nbsp;multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is multiple&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;only when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is odd.</p><p>There are total&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn></math>&nbsp;odd two-digit numbers.</p><p>Hence, the required&nbsp;probability&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>45</mn></mmultiscripts><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}